<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31127" root="عوه" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ عَائِهٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَاهٌ</span></b>  are like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَائِهٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاهٌ</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ عاه</span> is like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَبْشٌ ضانٌ</span> [so in my original,
but correctly <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَائِهٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَائِنٌ</span>: both app. mean <i>A
man having some moral bane</i> or <i>malady</i>]: accord.
to IAar, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَاهُونَ</span> [the pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَاهٌ</span>] signifies persons
<i>having in them what occasions suspicion,</i> and <i>what
is evil,</i> or <i>corrupt.</i> (TA.)

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
